mantle rm287
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_florence_gullworth
title the whittled landing
fits stage=adult|old
prefers quarter=sump
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk carves_a_stair_for_each_landing_worth_resting_on
likes roast_pork whittling fresh_straw first_warm_day
dislikes drizzle stale_bread
fears the_wharf_taking_even_the_good_memories
hopes a_little_wooden_stair_that_climbs_into_sun
topics memories +0.5 pastimes +0.5 home +0.4 faith +0.2
styles comfort=playful gossip=curious refuse=dry tease=light
marks oath saying
persona persona #self.first# skips a tread on the real stairs and shaves a broad seat into each landing of a pocket-sized wooden stair.

words
oath! = Splinter my best landing | Turn my shavings uphill
saying! = A short stair can have a long view | Every second tread saves a bit of sole
shaver = a keen little knife | a thumb-worn blade
curl = a shaving like a ring | a pale wood curl
step = a thin tread | a wooden step
landing = a shelf for sitting | a broad landing
peg = a tiny peg | a sliver of dowel
porkedge = a crisp edge of rind | a curl of crackling
strawstem = a new straw stem | a bright length of straw
breadheel = a hard bread heel | a crust with sharp corners
suncut = a slant of sun | a wedge of light
railtop = the polished rail | a smooth length of banister
tick = a shallow cut | a little nick
split = a split up the grain | a long pale crack

any
opinion houses against 3 : You can count freight and still leave out the wolf who didn't come home. I keep a different reckoning.
opinion sump for 2 : A bad step gets a name and a worse step gets a joke. That's how we make it upstairs.
opinion dole for 2 : A hot dish belongs at the top as much as the bottom. Someone ought to carry it all the way.
opinion festivals for 1 : I like seeing the heads come by underneath my window, particularly the ones with foolish hats.
opinion merchants against 1 : Rind oughtn't cost as much as the pork it once kept warm.
opinion road mixed 1 : A path going uphill will at least fetch you a view. The rest have to earn their keep otherwise.

grown
line greet : There's a seat for two if you take the sunny half. | Welcome to the level bit.
line greet.return : There's your welcome coming up two steps together. | I was hoping that greeting would reach my landing.
line again.open : Round again. I thought I knew those feet.
line farewell : Go steady where the third tread sticks out. | Save a good resting place for the way back.
line farewell.return : And a polished rail for your downward trip. | You've sent me off smiling at my feet.
line react.news : Let's hear how it sounds from up here. | Tell it while the shavings settle.
line react.news.new : That's a fresh notch entirely.
line react.news.known : I know which stair that account squeaks on.
line react.news.doubt : Something's shaved too nearly smooth in that version.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Some names ought to be kept even when the boats are gone.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : Now there's a tune for coming up the last flight.
line ask.how : Which part of your day needs a seat?
line answer.how : About two steps ahead of the slow thoughts.
line sympathise : Sit wide and let the poor old boards carry this one.
line reassure : A staircase takes you up one honest inch at a time.
line refuse : I've promised my knife a little careful attention first.
line accept_decline : Fair. Nobody can climb another wolf's legs for a favour.
line preclose : Time to count my own stairs homeward.
line accept_preclose : Go on with a light hip and an easy knee.
line ack : Yes. Every little notch of it.

scene exchange1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I make the landing first on a little wooden stair. | A stair in my pocket can have any number of steps.
b : Why start halfway up? | How many this time?
a : A good seat deserves to decide what leads to it. | One fewer than I want to climb after supper.

scene exchange2
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like pork rind crisp enough to startle a sleeper. | I turn my plate to save the corner with the crackle.
b : Do you eat quietly otherwise? | Can you leave it till last?
a : Never got a complaint from the roast. | I can turn the plate. Patience is another trick.

scene exchange3
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New straw catches every pale shaving. | I slip a stalk under the foot of a wobbly stool.
b : Isn't that a nuisance? | Does that hold it?
a : Not if you sweep the two together. | It names the bad foot. A proper chip will follow.

scene exchange4
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A first mild day lets me quit leaning against warm walls. | In spring I like a stair that's warm on the way down.
b : Where do you sit instead? | Why down?
a : Where heat can get round both elbows. | I had to climb the cold side earlier to find out.

scene exchange5
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle spots my polished wood with little shocked faces. | This rain has no proper stride.
b : Will it swell? | Is it raining at all?
a : It'll swell bigger if I let my scowl join in. | Enough to take two steps back for my cloak.

scene exchange6
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tried whittling a stale crust. | Bread that knocks on the plate needs broth.
b : Did you ruin the knife? | A great deal?
a : No, the crust was too proud to notice. | Enough to make a knocking noise from inside a cup instead.

scene exchange7
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sit where the stair turns halfway. | I shave the outer edge of a toy tread round.
b : What can you see there? | To keep little ankles safe?
a : The faces coming up and the shoulders going down. | Some things deserve to be comfortable on principle.

scene exchange8
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can do a good day's watching from one square of sun. | I keep my hands busy while the world files by.
b : Anything in particular you're observing? | Do you miss much?
a : A better square when this one moves. | Only the bits that don't bear a second glance.

scene exchange9
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The city has more landings than anybody's drawn. | I judge a hillside by the resting places going up.
b : What counts as a landing? | Which one's best?
a : Flat enough to set your supper on without holding the dish. | The one with another resting place still in sight.

scene exchange10
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One old hurt makes the wharf a difficult view. | A house mark can carry weight far past the wood it's stamped on.
b : Want the shutter closed? | Too much weight?
a : No. I want my good view back in small pieces. | For me, sometimes. I still know what's mine to remember.

scene exchange11
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the shape of the story downstairs. | A story's feet go faster than a witness's feet.
b : What shape has it up here? | Can you catch either?
a : Much the same with the sharp bits worn smooth. | I prefer sitting down with the witness.

scene exchange12
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard weather for purses. I'm saving clean offcuts. | When the cupboard gets pinched I number my remaining comforts.
b : For the fire? | Is it a long list?
a : For all the little presents a purse can't buy. | Long enough to begin with a chair and some light.

scene exchange13
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take the scenic way between two floors. | My legs have an opinion on a very steep lane.
b : That's still stairs, isn't it? | What do they say?
a : The scenery's at every window. | Look busy at the next doorway and let us rest.

scene exchange14
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a bench above the damp and a low bar under my heels. | A perfect wooden staircase would finish nowhere at all.
b : Need much more? | Who'd climb it?
a : An unhurried bit of afternoon to put on it. | A wolf after a good view and no errand at the other end.

old

scene exchange16
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Old knees don't mind two treads if the rail's honest. | At my age I inspect a stool before trusting it.
b : Wouldn't one be easier? | For splinters?
a : I'd rather choose when I start being sensible. | For signs a younger backside has tested it recently.

scene exchange17
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember when the rail seemed higher than my head. | I can make a long afternoon out of an old wooden button.
b : Has it worn lower? | By remembering the coat?
a : It's got lower both ways. I grew and the rail wore down. | By remembering the climb when the coat wouldn't do up.

scene exchange18
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My little carving knife has outlasted its first handle. | I once wanted a knife so sharp it shaved a thought in half.
b : Is it still the same knife? | And now?
a : My paws have changed shape too. We still recognise each other. | Just sharp enough to leave my thoughts and thumb attached.

scene exchange19
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's room at my window for a friend with tired ankles. | Company lifts my landing about a foot.
b : What about lively ankles? | Does the building really rise?
a : They can fetch the second stool. | I stop feeling the last few stairs I had to climb.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I whittled a tiny flight with such pride in its straight treads I forgot to cut the bottom flat.
  : Put the thing down and it rocked from end to end like a boat that wanted launching.
  b : Did you flatten it?
  : I carved a seat. It's a rocking stair now, which is an invention no sensible wolf had asked for.

story tale2 [topic=food self.likes=roast_pork]
  : I saved a glorious bit of crackling under a wooden lid. It sounded like a drum whenever my elbow hit the table.
  : At supper I removed the lid with great ceremony.
  b : Was your prize still crisp?
  : Soft as a boot tongue. I crisped it again and ate it before any other clever notions came my way.

story tale3 [topic=home]
  : One cold day a pale wood shaving sailed out of my pocket as I went upstairs. It rose past my nose on a draught.
  : I chased it two steps at a time and found it waiting on the topmost sill.
  b : Did its excursion finish there?
  : I gave it the view. No sense begrudging the winner a decent place to sit.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little more sunshine and I'd hardly need my eyes for carving. | That shaving curled uphill all by itself.

rule @call2
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Soft wood for landings, sound wood for rails. | Leave me one good chip for the seat.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Drizzle looking for somewhere to sit as well. | No polishing a wet rail today.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Last good light goes on my knife edge. | That's enough little stairs for one evening.
dlg resident.hub : Welcome to a staircase small enough for your pocket.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you've climbed back into view.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Too late for a sharp knife. Quite early enough for a tale.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We'll leave a whole tread between our elbows.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none] : I give the world a good steady looking at. There's plenty it would slip by me otherwise.
dlg resident.job : I'm partial to work with a good sitting place midway through.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : News took the stairs up. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : This came off the lower landing. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Count the steps it climbed first.
dlg resident.bye : Two steps or one, whatever brings you home easy.

graft resident.hub
choice Who climbs a staircase that small? -> toy_stair
node toy_stair
say So far, a beetle, and it went up the side. I put a great deal of precise work into treads the creature didn't trouble to use.
free
choice Will you change them? -> toy_stair_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node toy_stair_again
say I'll carve in a little rail. If the next beetle uses that for a road I'll have pleased somebody twice.
choice Enjoy the next climber. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
